I’ve been asked by a lot of people on whether or not they should get the iPhone 18 Pro Max or iPhone DUO. If you are in the same boat, then this post is for you! Don’t fall into the hype trap unless you have the funds. Here are some objective truths between both phones:

1. The DUO has worse battery (4800 vs 5500 mAh);
2. Cameras (between 17e & base iPhone 17 quality);
3. Slightly lower sustained A20 Pro performance (either due to smaller VC cooling plate or TDP restrictions); 
4. Bad aspect ratio in gaming (got to talk to a few CCs who gamed on the DUO during Apple event, but this is nothing new with current Android foldables);
5. Display durability and device longevity is less than 18 Pro Max (even with their scratch resistant coating);
6. (Subjective) DUO has no FaceID; 
7. Lastly, DUO is heavier and more bulky (especially with protection cases). 

On the flip side the DUO offers multi-tasking and a portable iPad Mini experience (But ask yourself, how often are you multitasking on your iPad, tablet, or current device?). 

Therefore, you are objectively paying more for less if you choose the iPhone DUO over the 18 Pro Max. Hopefully this helps those “average consumers” who are not aware of these details and have been blowing up my DMs.

PS: If you have excess funds and or a tech enthusiast, this post does not apply to you!

