Charlotte is a wonderful human being with a huge and generous heart. She does everything to be happy, but also to share some of that happiness with others. She wasn't born an artist, and for many years she didn't even knew she would be one, but she was destined to be a star. And although destiny has strange ways of showing you its path, she had the faith, intelligence, strength, resilience and discipline necessary to recognize and develop her skills and perfect them. She has the humility to acknowledge that there is always something more to learn and something to improve, which is why I believe she will be one of the most outstanding stars in her country. The irony is that fame came to her before she was an artist in the truest sense of the word, since she had to experience that whole process differently than most artists. While others prepare for the path to becoming an artist in relative anonymity, she had to go through it all under the public and critical eye, as well as the pressure of not making mistakes while simultaneously meeting the demands and expectations of many people, including her boss, her fans, the press, and the haters. Her path hasn't been easy; in fact, it could be said that it's been very difficult. But even so, she has never lost her noble essence, her dignity, or her ethics. She has learned from her mistakes and has developed rapidly and extraordinarily, both personally and professionally. She is truly admirable, and for that reason and more, I am proud to be her fan. 🤍 

